{"id": "unknown-2026-10-08-008", "date": "2026-10-08", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 41, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Silkworm seed production & storage facility opens in India’s Assam", "content": "India has opened a new grainage building and cold storage facility at the CSB Silkworm Seed Production Centre in Jorhat, Assam, under NERTPS. \nThe facility can produce 3 million disease-free layings of mulberry hybrid seed a year and preserve up to 10 million DFLs. \nAssam accounts for about 79 per cent of India’s muga silk and 74 per cent of eri silk production. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/silkworm-seed-production-storage-facility-opens-in-india-s-assam-314101-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-08-009", "date": "2026-10-08", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 41, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "India-EFTA pact covers 99.6% of exports: Commerce Secretary", "content": "India has urged exporters and industry bodies to make greater use of the India-EFTA TEPA, which covers 99.6 per cent of India’s exports through EFTA commitments.\nCommerce Secretary Rajesh Agrawal said EFTA commitments cover 92.2 per cent of tariff lines, while India covers 82.7 per cent.\nHe called for five-year market action plans and deeper value-chain partnerships.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/india-efta-pact-covers-99-6-of-exports-commerce-secretary-314096-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-08-010", "date": "2026-10-08", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 41, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "India’s cotton sector calls for price stability and assured supply", "content": "CITI held the 5th Global Cotton Conference in New Delhi on October 7, focusing on sustainable, traceable and higher-productivity cotton. \nMoUs covered ELS cotton, CottonConnect, FLA and TEXPROCIL links, while industry sought stable pricing and availability policies. \nIndia approved ₹5,659.22 crore (~$584 million) for cotton productivity and targets $100 billion in exports by 2030.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/india-s-cotton-sector-calls-for-price-stability-and-assured-supply-314093-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "lenzing-2026-10-08-011", "date": "2026-10-08", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 41, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": ["lenzing"], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["expand"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Lenzing and Kaihara showcase TENCEL fibres in REMOD denim range", "content": "Lenzing partnered with Japan’s Kaihara to launch the REMOD denim collection, showcasing three TENCEL Lyocell fibre types for cotton-inspired aesthetics, linen-like texture and softness.\nThe range will debut at Kingpins Amsterdam on October 14–15, 2026.\nLenzing’s HV100 mill network has expanded to nearly 50 mills across 13 countries, including Indian mills for the first time.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/lenzing-and-kaihara-showcase-tencel-fibres-in-remod-denim-range-314095-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-08-012", "date": "2026-10-08", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 41, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Barmag to present spinning and automation advances at India ITME 2026", "content": "Barmag will showcase POY 2.0 spinning, smart factory platforms and technologies for filaments, staple fibres and nonwovens at India ITME in Greater Noida on December 4–9, 2026.\nIts portfolio includes automatic string-up, digital traceability and flexible winding.\nThe company said its eFK EvoSmart texturing system could cut energy use by up to 25 per cent, supporting efficiency and lower production costs.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/barmag-to-present-spinning-and-automation-advances-at-india-itme-2026-314092-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-08-013", "date": "2026-10-08", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 41, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -1.0, "keywords": ["decline"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.65, "reasons": ["情緒極端"]}, "title": "Bangladesh's apparel exports to US rebound in August", "content": "Bangladesh's apparel exports to the US rose to $734.6 million in August 2026 from $660.9 million a year earlier, OTEXA data showed.\nChina and Vietnam posted modest gains, while Cambodia and India declined in August shipments to the US.\nFor January-August, Bangladesh shipments were about $5.39 billion, down 4.17 per cent from about $5.62 billion.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_apparel", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/apparel-news/bangladesh-s-apparel-exports-to-us-rebound-in-august-314087-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-08-014", "date": "2026-10-08", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 41, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Bangladesh-Russia apparel trade falls 61.5%: Who takes the orders?", "content": "Bangladesh’s direct RMG exports to Russia fell 61.5 per cent from FY2020-21 to FY2025-26, with July-August FY2026-27 shipments down 33.95 per cent year on year.\nTexPro shows China, Türkiye, Italy and India recovered after 2022, shipping $4.71 billion in 2025, 9.2 per cent above 2021.\nPayment bans and unsettled routes remain the main constraint for exporters.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_apparel", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/apparel-news/bangladesh-russia-apparel-trade-falls-61-5-who-takes-the-orders--314079-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
